@host = http://localhost:5099

### List clients (paged + filter). Try ?keyword=Acme&status=ActiveClient&page=1&pageSize=20
GET {{host}}/api/clients?pageSize=20

### Get one client (replace the id with one from the list)
GET {{host}}/api/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### Create an individual client
POST {{host}}/api/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientType": "Individual",
  "status": "ActiveClient",
  "firstName": "Alice",
  "lastName": "Walker",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "phone": "+61 400 555 111",
  "address": { "city": "Brisbane", "state": "QLD", "country": "Australia" }
}

### Create an organization client
POST {{host}}/api/clients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientType": "Organization",
  "status": "NewIntake",
  "organizationName": "Globex Corporation",
  "companyNumber": "99 888 777 666",
  "email": "legal@globex.example"
}

### Update a client
PUT {{host}}/api/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "OnHold",
  "firstName": "Alice",
  "lastName": "Walker",
  "phone": "+61 400 999 000"
}

### Add a contact to a client
POST {{host}}/api/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ID/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob Vance",
  "relationshipType": "Billing Contact",
  "email": "bob@example.com"
}

### Archive a client
POST {{host}}/api/clients/REPLACE_WITH_ID/archive
